{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/797474-a-question-about-knacks","id":797474,"title":"A Question About Knacks","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-31T13:00:56-08:00","id":797474,"title":"A Question About Knacks","content":"So I've just gotten my hands on Scion: God and flipped through the book and found a curious Stamina Knack that allows the character to halt their physical aging (I was under the impression this happened automatically at Demigod level). But once you become a god, you cease to age anyways.<br /> <br /> So my question regarding Knacks is that we can obtain these in <b>any order</b> so long as we have the prerequisite Knacks, right? For example, I could make a Hero with the Extended Youth Knack at character creation by taking Epic Stamina?<br /> <br /> Prior to getting the book, I mistook the knacks in each of them to be akin to that level of Legend, but that doesn't seem to be the case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 01-01-2016, 02:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T14:17:00-08:00","id":797506,"title":"","content":"Unless a Knack specifically lists pre-requisites, yes, they can be obtained at any time, in any order. Knacks that appear in God are not specific to Gods <i>unless they specifically say so.</i> Which means that, yes, a Hero can take Extended Youth. But... that's kinda pointless. It's basically an NPC-only trait. There's not going to be a big call for Scion games that span centuries <i>without</i> reaching a high enough Legend rating that it's not necessary. And if your game <i>does</i> focus on that... why are you charging the PC's XP for <i>your</i> idea?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T09:35:58-08:00","id":797852,"title":"","content":"We had a starting PC Hero take it for her character concept. She had been around for a long time. She was the daughter of Bastet. Her mother and her had a sort of mother cat/kitten relationship for several decades before start-of-game. Not that she was kept a child, she was just indulged and didn't really have much in the way of difficulties in getting what she wanted. She had to grow up pretty fast once the shit hit the fan at the start of game. <br /> <br /> There was a very cool scene in Bastet's old &quot;lair&quot;, a Roaring 20's Art Deco/Egyptian themed ruined luxury spa-hotel in the desert outside of Phoenix, AZ, where the other characters were looking at the pictures on the walls and saw their compatriot partying it up as a flapper.... <br /> <br /> If we had gotten to God, I would have let her switch it out for another Knack. I was also prepared to give her some more mechanical advantage if, say, they ended up<br /> fighting &quot;Old Age&quot; the Sorrows from Pandora's Jar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T11:05:14-08:00","id":797872,"title":"","content":"Thanks. By the way, I also have a question about Boons. Now I'm sure this is probably explained in the book somewhere, but I haven't gotten around to finding it yet.<br /> <br /> <br /> Gods don't <b>need</b> Relics to wield their Purviews, right? Or does that only apply to Purviews that are associated with them? The pre-made characters are all Gods, yet the book still says their Relics allow them access to such-and-such purview. Which leaves me a tad confused, since I thought I read somewhere in Hero or Demigod that you don't need relics after becoming a deity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T12:40:46-08:00","id":797922,"title":"","content":"I want to preface this answer with the fact that I haven't read the raw books in a while so I could be entirely wrong. That said, I'm pretty sure Gods don't need relics to channel a purview but not having the relic restricts the level of boons you can use. With a relic a god can use boons with a rating up to Legend - 1, while without a relic you can use boons with a rating up to Legend - 2. Like I said, I could be wrong about that, but I'm pretty sure that's right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4010-thenotorioussmp","name":"TheNotoriousSMP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T14:21:42-08:00","id":797976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheNotoriousSMP</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/797474-a-question-about-knacks?p=797922#post797922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to preface this answer with the fact that I haven't read the raw books in a while so I could be entirely wrong. That said, I'm pretty sure Gods don't need relics to channel a purview but not having the relic restricts the level of boons you can use. With a relic a god can use boons with a rating up to Legend - 1, while without a relic you can use boons with a rating up to Legend - 2. Like I said, I could be wrong about that, but I'm pretty sure that's right.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think that weakness applies to Demigods. In fact, I'm pretty sure that's where I read about it. When I was reading Hero, I found a detail that was something along the lines of &quot;Only the gods don't need Relics to channel their powers&quot; Hence my confusion as to why it specifically points out these Gods still keep Relics that grant them access.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}